Overview
Phone Book is a desktop contact-management application with a modern Persian user interface. It keeps the graphical interface separate from the database layer, making the project easier to understand, maintain, and extend.
Users can create contact groups, add and edit contacts, search by name or phone number, filter contacts by group, and safely remove records through confirmation dialogs.
Features
Add, edit, view, and delete contacts
Store first name, last name, phone number, email, and group
Search contacts by name or phone number
Create and delete contact groups
Filter the contact table by group
Prevent duplicate group names through the database layer
Protect non-empty groups from accidental deletion
Validate required contact fields before saving
Confirm destructive actions before deletion
Display clear success and error messages in the application
Close the database connection safely when the window exits
Responsive desktop layout with a scrollable contact table
Persian, right-aligned user interface
Tech Stack
Technology	Purpose
Python	Application logic
CustomTkinter	Modern desktop interface
Tkinter `ttk`	Contact table and scrollbar
SQLite	Local data persistence
Project Structure
```text
phone-book/
├── main.py          # Application window, interface, and event handling
├── database.py      # SQLite connection, schema, and CRUD operations
├── requirements.txt # Python dependencies (recommended)
├── .gitignore       # Files excluded from Git
└── README.md        # Project documentation
```
The application expects `database.py` to provide a `Database` class with the following methods:
```text
get_groups()
add_group(name)
delete_group(group_id)
get_contacts(group_id=None)
search_contacts(text)
get_contact(contact_id)
add_contact(first_name, last_name, phone, email, group_id)
update_contact(contact_id, first_name, last_name, phone, email, group_id)
delete_contact(contact_id)
close()
```
Getting Started
Prerequisites
Python 3.10 or newer
`pip`
Tkinter support
> Tkinter is included with most Windows and macOS Python installations. Some Linux distributions require it to be installed separately.
1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/YOUR-REPOSITORY.git
cd YOUR-REPOSITORY
```
Replace the example URL with the actual URL of this repository.
2. Create a virtual environment
Windows (PowerShell):
```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```
macOS or Linux:
```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```
3. Install the dependency
```bash
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install customtkinter
```
On Debian- or Ubuntu-based Linux systems, install Tkinter if it is missing:
```bash
sudo apt install python3-tk
```
4. Run the application
```bash
python main.py
```
How to Use
Enter a name in the sidebar and select افزودن گروه to create a group.
Enter the contact details in the form below the table.
Select افزودن مخاطب to save the new contact.
Select a row to load that contact into the form.
Edit the values and select ذخیره تغییرات to save the changes.
Use the search field to find a contact by name or phone number.
Select a group in the sidebar to display only its contacts.
Use نمایش همه to clear the current search and group filter.
Application Design
The project follows a simple two-layer structure:
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U["User"] --> G["CustomTkinter interface"]
    G --> D["Database class"]
    D --> S[("SQLite database")]
```
`main.py` builds the interface, validates user input, and handles events.
`database.py` owns SQL execution, transactions, and persistent storage.
SQLite stores the data locally, so no external database server is required.
Keeping these responsibilities separate prevents SQL details from leaking into the interface code and makes both layers easier to test.
Input and Deletion Rules
First name and phone number are required.
Last name, email, and group are optional.
An existing group name cannot be added again.
A group containing contacts cannot be deleted.
Contact and group deletion require user confirmation.
Database errors are caught and shown in the status area instead of crashing the interface.
Recommended `requirements.txt`
Create a `requirements.txt` file with:
```text
customtkinter>=5.2,<6.0
```
Then dependencies can be installed with:
```bash
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```
Suggested `.gitignore`
```gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
logs/
*.log
```
If a sample database is intentionally part of the repository, remove its extension from the ignore rules above.
Troubleshooting
`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'customtkinter'`
Activate the project virtual environment, then run:
```bash
python -m pip install customtkinter
```
`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'database'`
Make sure `database.py` is in the same directory as `main.py` and contains the `Database` class.
Tkinter is unavailable on Linux
Install the Tkinter package supplied by your Linux distribution. For Debian or Ubuntu:
```bash
sudo apt install python3-tk
```
Persian text is displayed with an unsuitable font
The interface uses Tahoma. Install Tahoma or replace the `FONT`, `FONT_BOLD`, and `FONT_TITLE` constants in `main.py` with another Persian-compatible font available on the system.
